    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d824">

                <pb facs="0945" n="933" sameAs="frus:frus1943v02/pg933"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/30253: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Hayes</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-07-24T20:00:00-04:00">July 24, 1943—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1582. Your 1894, 21st. You may refer to the message contained in Radio Bulletin
                    169, July 16 and to the President’s statement contained in Radio Bulletin 175,
                    July 23.<anchor n="37" xml:id="d824-f1"/> No assurance can be furnished of <pb
                        facs="0946" n="934" xml:id="pg934"/> course that there will be no repetition
                    inasmuch as decision in this regard must depend upon military necessity and upon
                    Italian action. The responsibilitiy clearly rests with Italy and it may be
                    pointed out that the Axis has exhibited no compunction over a period of years
                    about the destruction carried out wantonly by its forces, of Christian shrines
                    in a number of countries. It is not recalled incidentally that the Spanish
                    Episcopacy ever protested against the unchristian acts that have characterized
                    Axis warfare. Our bombing of Rome, made necessary by the Italian Government, was
                    carried out with great care to inflict as little damage as possible on cultural
                    monuments and church property, and it may be remarked that from this as well as
                    from the military standpoint the raid was remarkably successful.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d824-f1" n="37" xml:id="d824-f1-content">
                <p>Radio Bulletin No. 169 quotes text of the joint message of President Roosevelt
                    and Prime Minister Churchill to the people of Italy on July 16, 1943; for text,
                    see <ref target="#pg330">p. 330</ref>. The President’s statement in Radio
                    Bulletin No. 175 was to the effect that the United States in order to save
                    American and British lives would take what steps were necessary to prevent Axis
                    traffic through Rome from operating.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
